* feat(hooks): message:sending pre-send gate API

Adds a synchronous-blocking pre-send gate event so consumers (the
pr-gate workspace plugin and any other rule enforcement) can intercept
outbound message(send) calls before delivery.

- InternalHookEventKey: add "message:sending".
- MessageSendingGateContext, Handler, Decision types.
- registerMessageSendingGate / unregisterMessageSendingGate /
  clearMessageSendingGates / getMessageSendingGateHandlerCount.
- gateMessageSending — runs handlers in registration order, first
  blocking decision short-circuits.
- MessageBlockedError — typed error surfaces the gate reason to
  the agent harness.

Default-allow when no handlers are registered. Handler errors are
logged and do not block the send.

Part of RFC #33 (DarojaAI/.github#33): rule text + tool-hook
specification across darojaai_architect#41, daroja-coding-agent#20,
dev-nexus#1410 already merged. This commit is the API surface;
follow-up commits wire the gate into the outbound send site and
ship the pr-gate workspace plugin.

* feat(outbound): wire message-sending gate into executeSendAction

Calls `gateMessageSending` at the top of `executeSendAction` before
plugin dispatch and core delivery. If any handler returns
`allow: false`, throws `MessageBlockedError` so the agent harness
surfaces the reason to the model rather than silently dropping the
message.

Default-allow when no handlers are registered; the gate is opt-in.
A handler error logs and continues; only an explicit block decision
blocks.

Part of RFC DarojaAI/.github#33 (DarojaAI/openclaw#1 lands the API).

